Context: SDD

Purpose:
  Context Router and Token Optimization Engine. Defines how AI
  selects minimum sufficient context for any task, request, or
  mode. Prevents loading entire .sdd/ by using progressive context
  loading, priority-based selection, and dependency-aware routing.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1  @routing.sdd
   2  @priorities.sdd
   3  @budgets.sdd
   4  @loading.sdd
   5  @dependencies.sdd
   6  @cache.sdd

Modes:
  TASK       — task-specific context
  INCIDENT   — incident-specific context
  SECURITY   — security-specific context
  MANAGER    — manager/status context
  DEVELOPER  — developer/implementation context
  AUDIT      — full-project analysis (exception mode)

Rules:
  [CTX1]  AI MUST load minimum sufficient context for the current task.
  [CTX2]  AI MUST NEVER load entire .sdd/ unless explicit audit,
          architecture review, migration planning, or system-wide analysis.
  [CTX3]  Context expansion MUST be progressive: P0 → P1 → P2 → ...
  [CTX4]  Context confidence MUST be assessed before execution.
  [CTX5]  Stale or invalidated context MUST be rebuilt, not reused.
  [CTX6]  Context budget is determined by project level (L0-L5), not
          by arbitrary limits.
  [CTX7]  Context efficiency target: Relevant Context / Total Context > 80%.
  [CTX8]  Context miss MUST trigger EXPAND_CONTEXT, not silent failure.
  [CTX9]  Context audit metadata MUST be recorded for every session.
  [CTX10] Full project analysis is an exception mode, not default.

Entry:
  Read:
    INDEX.sdd

  Resolve:
    routing
    priorities
    budgets
    loading
    dependencies
    cache

Navigation:
  Context: @context/INDEX.sdd
  Routing: @context/routing.sdd
  Priorities: @context/priorities.sdd
  Budgets: @context/budgets.sdd
  Loading: @context/loading.sdd
  Dependencies: @context/dependencies.sdd
  Cache: @context/cache.sdd
  ProjectContext: @project/context/INDEX.sdd

State: +
  